                <p>The most important takeaway is that TCM and Western medicine ask different questions and therefore provide different answers. TCM asks "Why is this person's pattern of symptoms occurring?" and seeks to restore balance. Western medicine asks "What is the specific pathological process?" and seeks to eliminate disease. Both approaches have documented strengths and limitations &#x2192 which is precisely why integrative medicine &#x2192 combining both approaches under coordinated care &#x2192 often produces superior outcomes to either approach alone.</p>
