                </table>

                <p>For international patients, a typical acupuncture treatment course in China might involve 10-20 sessions over several weeks for chronic conditions, representing a total investment of &#x00A5;800-&#x00A5;16,000 ($110-$2,200 USD) compared to $600-$3,000+ for equivalent treatment in Western countries. Many international patients combine TCM treatment with a broader medical tourism visit, making the incremental cost of acupuncture treatment quite reasonable in the context of their total trip expenses.</p>

